  "raw_text": "226\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg\n-\n4\n):\n \nJisas heven ra spirit uplika kum baku iwi kan naha tasba ra kau aisubi takras kan piua ra.\n \n–\n \nJesus was living\n\nas a spirit person in heaven before he was born on this earth.\n \n/ Jesús vivía como un esp\ní\nritu en el cielo antes de nacer en\n\nesta tierra.\n)\n\nSturi yamni\n \nsmalkaia spiritka ba\n \n–\n \nthe evangelizing spirit\n \n/ el espíritu\n \nde\n \nevangelizador\n\nSpun\n \n–\n \nsee/ver:\n \nIspun\n\nSrikbaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nSrikwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto splash, to sprinkle, to spatter, to spray\n \n/ pringar, salpicar, brisar, rociar\n\nSrikwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nSrikbaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto splash, to sprinkle, to spatter, to spray\n \n/ pringar, salpicar, brisar, rociar\n\nSrimaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go numb\n \n/ entumirse, entumecerse\n\nSringka\n \n(a/t:\n \nSrinhka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nnerve, nervousness, impetuousness, nervous fear, timidity\n \n/ nervio, nerviosismo,\nimpetuosidad, miedo nervioso, timidez\n\n(Construct:\n \nSringki\n \n–\n \nmy nervousness\n \n/ mi nerviosismo;\n \nSringkam\n \n–\n \nyour nervousness\n \n/ tu nerviosismo;\n \nAi sringka\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their\nnervousness\n \n/ su nerviosismo)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh17\n):\n \nHelp makabaia srinhka bripara\n \n–\n \nDo not have nervousness\n \n(alt:\n \nDo not be too nervous\n)\n \nto ask for help\n \n/ No tener\nnerviosismo (alt: No estar demasiado nervioso) para pedir ayuda)\n\nSringka âpu\n \n(\nwqu-02/20\n)\n \n–\n \nwithout timidity, without nervousness, without nervous fear\n \n/ sin timidez, sin\nnerviosismo, sin miedo nervioso\n\nSringkira\n \ndaukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto cause to be nervous/afraid, to be affected by nervousness/fear\n \n/ causar nerviosismo/\nmiedo, ser afectado por nerviosismo/miedo\n\nSringkira ai daukisa\n \n(\nsp\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nmakes me nervous\n \n/ me pone nervioso\n\nSringkikira\n \n(a/t:\n \nSrinhkikira\n,\n \nSringka kira\n-\ndb\n) (adv,adj)\n \n–\n \nnervously, impetuously, nervous, impetuous\n \n/ nervioso,\nimpetuoso\n\nSrinkaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nSrinwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto cause to be lazy, to relax, to lounge, to loiter\n \n/ causar ser perezoso, relajarse,\ndescansar, holgazanear\n\nSrinwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nSrinkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be lazy, to be idle\n \n/ ser perezoso, estar inactivo\n\nSrinwankira\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \nlazy, slack, idle\n \n/ perezoso, flojo, inactivo\n\nSriwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \n…\n \n/ …\n\nSriwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwrinkle\n \n/ arruga\n\nTaya sriwan\n \n–\n \nwrinkled skin\n \n/ piel arrugada\n\nSrukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto fold, to wrap, to envelope, to enwrap\n \n/ doblar, envolver\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlv-209\n):\n \nKristian mairin nani ba G\nȃ\nd warkka dauki, sam taim ai lal praki srukaia sa.\n \n–\n \nChristian women doing God’s work\n\nsometimes must cover their head (wear a head covering).\n \n/ Las mujeres cristianas que hacen la obra de Dios a veces deben\ncubrirse la cabeza.)\n\nSrutkaia\n \n(v-trans; intrans:\n \nSrutwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto cause to jump, to cause to leap, to cause to skip\n \n/ hacer saltar, hacer brincar\n\nSrutwaia\n \n(v-intrans; trans:\n \nSrutkaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto jump, to leap, to skip\n \n/ saltar, brincar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 35:6\n):\n \nSkahwa nani ba sula srutwi pâli baku srutwi kabia\n \n–\n \nThe lame will be leaping like a leaping deer\n \n/ Cojo\nsaltará como un ciervo saltando)\n\nStadi daukaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nTadi daukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto start a study with someone, to do a study\n \n/ comenzar un estudio con alguien,\nhacer un estudio\n\nStadi munaia\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nTadi munaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto study\n \n/ estudiar\n\nStadi tihu munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do deep study\n \n/ hacer un estudio profundo\n\nStadi takaia\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nTadi takaia\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto study\n \n/ estudiar\n\nBaibil stadi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto study the Bible, to have a Bible study\n \n/ estudiar la Biblia, tener un estudio bíblico\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmqu\n-\n05/19\n-\nstadika22\n):\n \nAhkia man taimkam sakisma Baibil stadi takaia dukiara?\n \n–\n \nWhen do you take out time in\n\norder to do Bible study?\n \n/ ¿Cuándo tomas tiempo para estudiar la Biblia?\n)\n\nBaibil stadi\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nBible study\n \n(in the ministry)\n \n/\n \ne\nstudio bíblico (en el ministerio)\n\nBaibil\n \nstadi tatakra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \nBible student, Bible study (person who studies the Bible)\n \n/\n\nestudiante de la Biblia, estudio de la Biblia (persona que estudia la Biblia)\n\n(Construct:\n \nBaibil stadi tatakriki, Baibil stadi tatakrikam)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n10/20\n):\n \nStadi tatakra ba aidrubanka nani ra wabia dukiara yawan nahki kupia bukaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nHow\n\nare we able to encourage the student to go to the meetings?\n \n/ ¿Qué podemos hacer para animar al estudiante a\n\nir a las reuniones?\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nJisas ba Dawan B\nî\nla stadi tatakra pain kum kan ba yawan nahki nu sa?\n \n–\n \nHow do we know that Jesus was a\n\ngood\n \nstudent of God’s Word?\n \n/ ¿Cómo sabemos que Jesús fue un buen estudiante de la Palabra de Dios?\n)",
